; The project-wide UI theme. Set as gui/theme/custom in project.godot, so every Control in the
; game inherits it without a single line of code.
;
; It carries ONE thing on purpose: the default faces and a sane default size. The type SCALE -
; Display / Title / Body / Label / Micro - lives in scripts/ResponsiveLayout.cs and stays there.
; Godot themes support type variations that could hold those sizes too, and putting them here as
; well would give the game two sources of truth for the same five numbers, which is exactly how
; thirteen different font sizes for five jobs happened in the first place.
;
; TWO FACES, and the rule for which is which:
;
;   PROSE - every Label, every description, every stat line - is the engine's own face (Open Sans
;   SemiBold, built into Godot, so nothing is added to assets/ or NOTICE). There is deliberately
;   no default_font below: leaving it unset is what selects it.
;
;   CARVED - headings only, ResponsiveLayout's Display and Title roles - is Cinzel at weight 700
;   (HeadingFont.tres). Buttons stay in the prose face: putting Cinzel on Button in this theme
;   would also put it on every CheckButton and CheckBox (they inherit Button's theme items), and
;   those carry whole sentences in the options screen.
;
; Why the prose stopped being Cinzel. Cinzel is cut from Roman inscriptional capitals; its lower
; case is a set of small capitals. A sentence in it is a sentence in all caps, with hairline
; strokes, and every menu in the game was set that way - the player's report was simply that the
; menus were hard to read. Pixelify Sans before it could not tell a 5 from an 8. A plain humanist
; sans at semibold has neither problem and is what a player reads fastest at 20-24px on a phone.
; See .ai/level-up-screen.md, "Legibility".
[gd_resource type="Theme" format=3]

[resource]
default_font_size = 20
